I'll review the assigned GitHub port files against the pinned upstream oracle and the round-1 inventory, and I'll only report new findings.Round 1 already closed a large set of findings. I'll check the pinned commit and the port notes, then look only for what those fixes left behind.I'll confirm the GraphQL record guard against the oracle and law 17 before writing the finding.### fable-2-1
- file: scratchpad/effected/github/GraphQL.ts:198
- class: type-safety   severity: required
- standard: D15 and D11 (the assertion scan counts `as`, `!`, `<T>expr`, and `any`, and misses a user-defined type predicate); standards/effect-laws-v1.md law 17 (derive guards with `S.is` or a built-in whose declared type matches the value); same gate miss as closed inventory req-30, which fixed `internal/octokit.ts:219` and left this site. evidence: `const isRecord = (value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> => P.isObjectOrArray(value)` at GraphQL.ts:198, used by `asRecord` (200–201) and `GitHubGraphQLError.fromThrowable` (175–186) for the throwable, `headers`, and `response.headers`. `Predicate.isObjectOrArray` (`~/YeeBois/references/effect/effect/packages/effect/src/Predicate.ts:1038`) is `typeof input === "object" && input !== null`, returns `{ [x: PropertyKey]: unknown } | Array<unknown>`, and its example states `Predicate.isObjectOrArray([])` is true. Oracle `asRecord` (`packages/github/src/GraphQL.ts:109–110`) is `typeof value === "object" && value !== null ? (value as Record<string, unknown>) : undefined`, so an array still passes at runtime; the `as` was replaced by a predicate that claims a record.
- failure: an array is narrowed to `Record<string, unknown>`. `status`, `headers`, `message`, `errors`, and `retryAfterMillisFrom` then read it as a string-keyed record. tsgo, oxlint, and the D15 scan stay green.
- fix: delete `isRecord` and narrow with `P.isObject` (`Predicate.ts:1071`, excludes arrays, declared `{ [x: PropertyKey]: unknown }`) before treating the value as a record. If refusing an array changes acceptance relative to the oracle cast, the cause is law 17 under section 14.

